{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<?ui-args --extension-package components/scxml-extension-example/package/example.extension.json?>\n<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\"\n       xmlns:example=\"https://stateforward.org/scxml/example\"\n       xmlns:env=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env\"\n       version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"s0\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"outcome\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"s0\">\n    <onentry>\n      <example:fetch url=\"https://api.example/v1/items\" location=\"outcome\" env:tokn=\"API_TOKEN\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"example.fetched\" target=\"done\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml083-env-slot-typo.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml083-env-slot-typo.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":4,"byteOffset":505,"endColumn":84,"endLine":11,"startColumn":80,"startLine":11},"insertedContent":{"text":"token"}}]}],"description":{"text":"bind the declared slot `token`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml083-env-slot-typo.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":96,"endLine":11,"startColumn":76,"startLine":11}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<example:fetch>` has no `env` slot `tokn`\n\n**Note:** the package of `https://stateforward.org/scxml/example` declares the slots `url`, `token`\n\n**Help:** did you mean `token`?\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §4.10 Extensibility of Executable Content","text":"`<example:fetch>` has no `env` slot `tokn`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":521,"start":501},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML083"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"an executable-content extension element names the variables whose values its host binds to it with `env:<slot>=\"NAME\"` (or `env:<slot>expr=\"EXPR\"`, an expression that evaluates to the name) in the `https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env` namespace; the host gives the extension component an opaque reference for each slot, never the value. The slots an element has are the ones its package manifest declares (`env-slots`); its schema admits the namespace with a lax wildcard, so only this rule catches a misspelled slot, a slot named twice (`env:<slot>` and `env:<slot>expr`), or an `env:<slot>` value that is not a variable name (`[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`). It is checked for every element whose package the validator was given. An invoked service's `<invoke>` binds the slots its service package declares the same way (`<invoke type=\"URI\" env:endpoint=\"ECHO_URL\">`), checked when the validator was given that package; the host binds those references for the whole invocation"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: bind only a slot the element's package declares, once, to a variable name.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §4.10 Extensibility of Executable Content\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML083` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#extensibility","id":"SCXML083","name":"SCXML083","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an `env` attribute names a slot its element does not have"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}